# The exact denial each document in storage-partial-persistent-volume.yaml must produce.
# scripts/test-policy-fixtures.sh compares this whole set: a message that
# disappears is a weakened rule, a message that appears is an unreviewed
# denial. File-level rejection alone hides both.
PersistentVolume <unnamed> has no usable spec mapping and cannot be evaluated
PersistentVolume <unnamed> must declare an enumerated storageClassName
PersistentVolume <unnamed> must declare exactly one volume source, found 0
